o  choose to have one less child because  that will that will reduce uh greenhouse  gas emissions carbon emissions over the  lifetime of that child and potentially  that child's children much more so than  if we do all those other good things you  know changing our light bulbs to low  energy light bulbs not flying giving up  our car taking a vegan diet but it's 20  times more impactful and if you look at  the science if you look at the reports  whether it's by Lunt University in  Sweden or Oregon State University  there's really good evidence of that  his organization firmly opposes any form  of coercive policy like those we heard  about in India or the one child rule  China recently discarded to address its  aging population  but it does ask people especially in the  Richer world to consider the planet when  they make decisions around Family  Planning  it's a sad reality that when it comes to  climate change the poorest parts of the  world are both the most at risk and the  least responsible they're also the areas  of the world where birth rates are  highest the tragedy is that you know the  number of women who have that unmet need  for safe Modern Family Planning has  increased by about 40 million over the  past decade due to population growth  in Africa and Southeast Asia similarly  the number of girls out of school has  increased in Africa by about seven eight  million because of population growth  it's a bit sensitive because for many of  us a man's wealth or a man's number of  blessings are counted by the number of  children and so in some of the religious  settings and some of the cultures Family  Planning is overlooked or perhaps  frowned upon but that being said within  the medical  within the medical sector within the  health sector I beg your pardon  you know at least at the Primary  Healthcare level it is still being uh  there's advocacy and there's guidance if  you want it research has shown that the  single biggest factor that correlates  with a decline in birth rates is female  education access to contraception and  GDP per capita also play a role  as the literacy goes up number of  children go down across communities  and as the income goes up the number of  children goes down again across  community  since the beginning of this video more  than 4 500 babies will have been born  around the world  some will be blessed with abundance and  others will struggle  some will be born into vibrant  communities full of young people and  others will enter societies that are  aging fast  all will live on a planet that has never  before been home to so many people  and that wraps up this edition of  business Beyond I'd love to know what  the demographic challenges are in your  part of the world do let us know in the  comments and if you like what you see  here check out our business Beyond  playlist a good place to start would be  our recent video on the challenges  facing big Tech  until next time from me and the team  it's goodbye and take care
 

